  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme uses a close-up of a man with a smug or condescending expression, juxtaposed with text that implies a parent (likely a mother) was fined for littering while dropping off their child at school. The intent is to mock or shame the parent for a minor infraction, potentially implying incompetence or irresponsibility. While not explicitly targeting a specific protected group, it can be perceived as demeaning to parents in general, especially mothers, by highlighting a trivial mistake in a judgmental way. This can be harmful as it may contribute to a culture of public shaming and could make parents feel embarrassed or judged for everyday mistakes, potentially damaging their self-esteem or social standing. The humor is derived from the absurdity of the situation, but the underlying message can be hurtful and discouraging.",
